# For docker-compose.local.yml. Copy to `.env.local` and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored. This example is not, and must never carry a real key.

# ── Required ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The PM agent has NO scripted double: all three of its operations call a model. Without a key
# the compose refuses to start, which is better than starting an agent that 502s every request.
#
# `openrouter/free` costs nothing. Give the key a credit limit in the OpenRouter dashboard
# anyway: it is the only ceiling that does not depend on this code behaving.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...

# One secret. Both agents are one process now (agente-backend/src/mirag_manager, service
# "mirag-agents" below) and validate every request against the same MIRAG_TOKEN, whichever
# prefix ("/backend" or "/pm") it arrives under — there is no longer a second process for a
# second token to belong to.
#
#   python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(24))"
MIRAG_TOKEN=local-cambiame

# ── Optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The models. Everything here depends on tool calling: the PM delivers a plan through a tool,
# the backend delivers a project through `specify_project` and `deliver_group`. A model that
# answers in prose produces an empty delivery and looks like a broken agent.
#
# Run `python scripts/probe_models.py` in agente_backend to re-decide this. Free models rotate
# and the two names that used to be here are both disproven by that probe today:
# `poolside/laguna-s-2.1:free` spends its whole budget reasoning and emits nothing (285s, no
# tool call), and `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` writes every file on a single line.
#
# DO NOT just take the top of the probe's table. The probe times ONE call; what matters is the
# whole run, and the two diverge. Measured end to end on the same idea:
#
#   inclusionai/ling-3.0-flash-sante:free   37s/call    176s total   19/19 files
#   inclusionai/ling-3.0-flash-vl:free      95s/call    463s total   PARTIAL
#   liquid/lfm-2.5-2.6b:free                15s/call    283s total   FAILED, 2 files never sent
#
# The fastest per call was the slowest overall: it returned tool-call JSON that would not
# parse, burned the group retries, and never delivered the tests. A model that delivers badly
# forces repairs, and every repair is another call in series.
# MIRAG_BACKEND_MODEL=inclusionai/ling-3.0-flash-sante:free
#
# The PM has NOT been probed with its own prompt. `probe_models.py` sends the backend's shape
# (`deliver_group`, the full contract, five files at once); the PM sends `ask_questions` and
# `deliver_plan`, which are prose fields rather than file bodies. The name below has only been
# validated indirectly, by runs that completed with a usable plan.
# MIRAG_PM_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free

# Per-request spending cap. Low on purpose for local work.
# MIRAG_BUDGET_USD=0.10
